WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.700
Welcome to Grade 7 English, Unit 7:
Success, Careers, and Personal Growth.

2
00:00:06.300 --> 00:00:10.580
Welcome to Unit 7: Success, Careers, and Personal Growth.

3
00:00:11.200 --> 00:00:16.180
In this unit you will explore what it means to
succeed, how people build meaningful careers,

4
00:00:16.680 --> 00:00:19.220
and how personal growth shapes the choices we make.

5
00:00:19.920 --> 00:00:25.200
You will read about real-world career paths,
discuss what makes a person truly successful,

6
00:00:25.700 --> 00:00:32.420
and discover that success is not only about money
or fame — it is also about dedication, resilience,

7
00:00:32.880 --> 00:00:35.220
and the contribution you make to your community.

8
00:00:36.020 --> 00:00:41.360
In this short lecture, preview the key
ideas and prepare for the independent lesson.

9
00:00:42.100 --> 00:00:47.900
By the end of this unit, you will be able to read
and understand a passage about careers and success,

10
00:00:47.900 --> 00:00:50.040
and discuss its ideas in english.

11
00:00:50.860 --> 00:00:59.280
you will also use adjective + preposition combinations
correctly (e.g., *interested in*, *proud of*, *responsible for*).

12
00:01:00.080 --> 00:01:06.660
you will also understand and use verb patterns
with infinitives (*to do*) and gerunds (*doing*).

13
00:01:07.400 --> 00:01:09.300
Keep these goals in mind as you work.

14
00:01:10.280 --> 00:01:18.940
Your vocabulary work begins with these words: ambition,
dedication, perseverance, achievement, milestone, distinction.

15
00:01:19.840 --> 00:01:24.540
Listen to each pronunciation in the
vocabulary lab, study its meaning in context,

16
00:01:25.040 --> 00:01:28.140
and use the word accurately in
your own discussion and writing.

17
00:01:28.860 --> 00:01:36.320
The reading sequence includes Success, Careers, and
Personal Growth: source text 1 and Success, Careers,

18
00:01:36.320 --> 00:01:39.010
and Personal Growth: source text 2.

19
00:01:39.620 --> 00:01:40.200
Read actively.

20
00:01:40.880 --> 00:01:45.380
Identify each text's central ideas,
notice viewpoint and reliability,

21
00:01:45.980 --> 00:01:49.240
and support every inference with
relevant evidence from the text.

22
00:01:49.940 --> 00:01:54.080
The first language focus is
Adjective + Preposition — The Basics.

23
00:01:55.460 --> 00:02:01.860
What it means and why it matters In English, many
adjectives must be followed by a specific preposition.

24
00:02:02.580 --> 00:02:07.080
You cannot choose just any preposition
— each adjective has a fixed partner.

25
00:02:07.680 --> 00:02:13.980
For example, we say interested in (not
“interested about”) and proud of (not “proud for”).

26
00:02:14.820 --> 00:02:21.680
Learning these pairs will make your English sound natural
and help you write accurately about success, careers,

27
00:02:22.020 --> 00:02:23.260
and personal growth.

28
00:02:23.940 --> 00:02:29.820
Notice the structure in the model examples, then apply
it deliberately in connected sentences and paragraphs.

29
00:02:30.740 --> 00:02:35.120
In speaking, you will complete
Speaking 1: Vocabulary Expert Interview.

30
00:02:35.620 --> 00:02:39.960
Organise your ideas, use evidence
and respond clearly to questions.

31
00:02:40.440 --> 00:02:43.120
In writing, you will plan, draft, check and revise.

32
00:02:43.860 --> 00:02:46.370
Use the success criteria before submitting your work.

33
00:02:46.620 --> 00:02:48.300
You are ready to begin.

34
00:02:48.820 --> 00:02:54.480
Start with the vocabulary lab, continue through
reading and comprehension, apply the grammar focus,

35
00:02:54.920 --> 00:02:57.020
and complete the speaking and writing practices.

36
00:02:57.740 --> 00:03:02.980
Use AI English for hints and feedback, and
bring your questions to the live sessions.
